{
  "$comment": "The stage ledger (E30): the 1.3.0 plan's stages in release order, D20's numbering in `planned` (each stage as the next 1.2.X, the last as 1.3.0; retired by O1 on 15.10.2026: a release is a train of several stages, each train the next 1.2.X). A stage has shipped when `version` is set and module.json's version is at or past it, compared number by number. `version` and `shipped` (a UTC date) are written only by `node tools/stages.mjs ship <id> [<id> ...]`, in the release commit, one version and one date to every stage of the train; `planned` is information. `touches` is what a stage's release changes among sockets, rolls and scenes (null: not declared), `drills` the local-gate drills it names. The rows E65, E66, E68, E69, E71, E73 and E74 came with E65 (its plan, 30.10.2026), and E65's C0 renumbered the `planned` of every unshipped row after E50's train one per row from E65's 1.2.95 (Q-E65-2; E26 stays 1.3.0): information only, the release numbers are the owner's. E96 C1 (09.11.2026) put the hotfix E96 (1.2.102) before E46 and wrote the owner's order of 09.11.2026: E46 with E47 1.2.103, E95 1.2.104, E68 1.2.105, then the other unshipped rows in their order, one version each (E62 with E61). E47-FD (10.11.2026) wrote the owner's plan for the case map of 09.11.2026: E97 1.2.108, E98 1.2.109 and E99 1.2.110 before E61, and every unshipped row from E61 on three versions later (E61 and E62 1.2.111; E26 stays 1.3.0). The regroup of 10.11.2026 (the owner): E68 ships with E95 as 1.2.104, E49 with E48 as 1.2.105, and every unshipped row after them moves two versions down (E97 1.2.106, E98 1.2.107, E99 1.2.108, E61 and E62 1.2.109; E26 stays 1.3.0). Later on 10.11.2026 the owner moved E99 after E62: E61 and E62 1.2.108, E99 1.2.109, the rows after them unchanged. On 11.11.2026 the owner put E98 with E97 as 1.2.106 and E63 (the body tile's rules, from the owner's answers to E95's Q2, Q3 and Q8: a tile at every death, an execution too, removed at a revive and at the end of a Class Trial) in E48's train as 1.2.105 (its `with` the row above, E49), and every unshipped row after E98 moved one version earlier (E61 and E62 1.2.107, E99 1.2.108; E26 stays 1.3.0). On 12.11.2026 the owner put E76 next as 1.2.106, E97 and E98 1.2.107, E61 and E62 1.2.108, E99 1.2.109, then E92, E94, E64, E93, E69, E74, E73, E72, E54, E55, E56, E25, E71, E91, E57 and E59 in that order, one version each (1.2.110-1.2.125), and deferred E38, E39, E40, E43, E53 and E58 to a local session on a machine with Foundry v14, right before E83: 1.2.126-1.2.131, E83 1.2.132 (E26 stays 1.3.0); the rows are moved into that order. On 12.11.2026 E73 and E99 took 1.2.108 because they were ready first (the owner's \"Zgoda\" of 12.11.2026): E73 moved up from 1.2.116 with E99 `with` it, and the curtain train, E61 and E62, became 1.2.109; E92 (the Spectator), built on the curtain line, moved up from 1.2.110 to ship with it as 1.2.109, `with` E62 (the coordinator, 12.11.2026); 1.2.110 and 1.2.116 are left empty and the rows after them unchanged. Later on 12.11.2026 E94 (all of it, from 1.2.111) joined the 1.2.109 train after E92, `with` E92, so E61, E62, E92 and E94 stand in that order, each `with` the row directly above it; `node tools/stages.mjs ship E61 E62 E92` writes all four (a `ship` names every row the next row's `with` points at; tried on a copy, 12.11.2026), and the rows after E94 keep their `planned`. On 12.11.2026 E72 and E91 joined E64 as 1.2.110 (the coordinator): E64 moved up from 1.2.112, E72 from 1.2.117 and E91 from 1.2.123, their rows moved up under E64's, E72 `with` E64 and E91 `with` E72, and the rows between them keep their `planned`. On 14.11.2026 the owner's plan changed again and was written: every cloud stage ships in 1.2.113 - E54, E38, E55, E56, E25, E71, E57 and E102, in that order, each `with` the row directly above it; 1.2.114 is released after the local-Foundry stages and the audit - E59, E39, E40, E43, E53, E58 and E83, the same way; E26 stays 1.3.0, released after the owner's review. E55's and E43's rows moved into these places. Read by the suite (expectedRed and DUMP_RULES `until`), by `node tools/stages.mjs check` and by the release gate.",
